; ============================================================
; 2026.bean — Transactions for 2026
;
; 1. Purpose: This file contains all financial transactions for the year 2026.
; 2. Beneficiary rules:
;       - Do not write the ledger owner's name for beneficiaries.
;       - Leave your own expenses without a beneficiary tag (implicitly yours).
;       - Tag other people using the beneficiary tag indented under their 
;       specific expense line.
;       - For split expenses, create separate posting lines and tag only 
;       the other person on their respective line.
; 3. Metadata and formatting rules:
;       - Location specific metadata (such as beneficiary or property) under 
;       the specific posting line, never under the main transaction header.
;       - Start every transaction date at the absolute left margin with 
;       no indentation.
;       - Keep narrations short and concise. Use the note tag on the 
;       following line for long explanations or context.
;       - Omit the time and location lines entirely if specific transaction 
;       details are unknown.
;       - Do not repeat account names or line amounts in the main narration 
;       if the data is already in the posting lines.
; 4. Chronological sorting:
;       - Keep all transactions strictly organized in chronological order by date.
; 5. Tag standardization:
;       - Write all standard custom metadata values (such as transport_mode) 
;       entirely in lowercase.
;       - Maintain correct capitalization and spelling for proper nouns inside 
;       tags (such as beneficiary names or specific property locations).
; 6. Transport mode tracking:
;       - Use the transport_mode tag indented under transport posting lines 
;       to track the specific vehicle type.
; ============================================================

